   "source": [
    "# LendingClub Interest Rate Prediction\\n",
    "## MSBA Machine Learning Project\\n",
    "\\n",
    "**Team:** [Your Team Number] | **Section:** [Your Section] | **Date:** May 2026\\n",
    "\\n",
    "This notebook presents a comprehensive machine learning pipeline to predict loan interest rates using the LendingClub dataset. The pipeline includes: (1) data preprocessing with zero leakage, (2) temporal train/validation/test splits, (3) feature engineering, (4) training and comparison of five models (three gradient boosting + two neural networks), (5) ensemble methods, and (6) model explainability analysis.\\n",
    "\\n",
    "### Anti-Leakage & Anti-Temporal-Bias Design\\n",
    "- **No data leakage**: All features verified to be available at loan origination; `loan_status` (post-origination outcome) removed\\n",
    "- **No temporal bias**: Temporal split (70/15/15) with older loans for training, newer for testing; simulates real-world deployment\\n",
    "- **Preprocessing integrity**: All transformations fit on training data only"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup & Data Loading"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\\n",
    "import numpy as np\\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\\n",
    "import warnings\\n",
    "import pickle\\n",
    "import os\\n",
    "from sklearn.base import BaseEstimator, TransformerMixin\\n",
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error, mean_absolute_error, r2_score\\n",
    "from sklearn.inspection import permutation_importance, partial_dependence\\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\\n",
    "import xgboost as xgb\\n",
    "import lightgbm as lgb\\n",
    "import catboost as cb\\n",
    "import shap\\n",
    "import torch\\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import TensorDataset, DataLoader\\n",
    "\\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "# LOAD DATA\\n",
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "train_df = pd.read_csv('LC_train.csv')\\n",
    "test_df = pd.read_csv('LC_test.csv')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(f\\"Train shape: {train_df.shape}\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"Test shape: {test_df.shape}\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"Target (int_rate): mean={train_df['int_rate'].mean():.2f}%, std={train_df['int_rate'].std():.2f}%\\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Data Leakage Audit\\n",
    "\\n",
    "We carefully audit all features to ensure they are available at loan origination time. Features that represent post-origination outcomes must be excluded."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "# LEAKAGE AUDIT\\n",
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# LEAKAGE FEATURES TO REMOVE:\\n",
    "# 1. loan_status: POST-ORIGINATION outcome (Current, Fully Paid, Charged Off, Late, etc.)\\n",
    "#    This describes what HAPPENED to the loan AFTER funding.\\n",
    "#    Using it to PREDICT the interest rate that was set BEFORE funding is circular logic.\\n",
    "# 2. title: Redundant with purpose (free-text version of the same categorical info)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "LEAKAGE_FEATURES = ['loan_status', 'title']\\n",
    "print(\\"Features removed due to leakage risk:\\")\\n",
    "for feat in LEAKAGE_FEATURES:\\n",
    "    print(f\\"  - {feat}: {'POST-ORIGINATION outcome' if feat == 'loan_status' else 'Redundant with purpose'}\\")\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Separate target and features\\n",
    "y = train_df['int_rate'].copy()\\n",
    "train_features = train_df.drop(columns=LEAKAGE_FEATURES + ['int_rate']).copy()\\n",
    "test_features = test_df.drop(columns=[c for c in LEAKAGE_FEATURES if c in test_df.columns]).copy()\\n",
    "test_ids = test_features.pop('ID') if 'ID' in test_features.columns else test_df['ID']\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(f\\"\\nRemaining {len(train_features.columns)} features verified at origination:\\")\\n",
    "print(list(train_features.columns))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Temporal Train/Validation/Test Split\\n",
    "\\n",
    "We use a temporal split (not random) to simulate real-world deployment: train on past loans, validate on recent loans, test on newest loans. The data is ordered by time (index serves as temporal proxy)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "# TEMPORAL SPLIT (NO RANDOM SHUFFLE)\\n",
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "n = len(train_features)\\n",
    "train_end = int(n * 0.70)  # 70% training\\n",
    "val_end = int(n * 0.85)    # 15% validation, 15% test\\n",
    "\\n",
    "X_train = train_features.iloc[:train_end].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\\n",
    "X_val = train_features.iloc[train_end:val_end].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\\n",
    "X_test = train_features.iloc[val_end:].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\\n",
    "y_train = y.iloc[:train_end].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\\n",
    "y_val = y.iloc[train_end:val_end].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\\n",
    "y_test = y.iloc[val_end:].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(f\\"Temporal Split: Train={len(X_train):,} | Val={len(X_val):,} | Test={len(X_test):,}\\")\\n",
    "print(f\\"Mean int_rate - Train: {y_train.mean():.3f}% | Val: {y_val.mean():.3f}% | Test: {y_test.mean():.3f}%\\")\\n",
    "print(\\"(Slight drift confirms temporal ordering)\\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Feature Engineering\\n",
    "\\n",
    "We create 29 new domain-informed features from the original 36, resulting in 58 total features. All transformations use only training data statistics to prevent leakage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "# CUSTOM FEATURE ENGINEERING\\n",
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "class LendingClubPreprocessor(BaseEstimator, TransformerMixin):\\n",
    "    \\\\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\\n",
    "        self.top_emp_titles = None\\n",
    "    \\\\n",
    "    def fit(self, X, y=None):\\n",
    "        # Learn top 40 employment titles from training data\\n",
    "        emp_title_clean = X['emp_title'].fillna('Unknown').str.lower().str.strip()\\n",
    "        meaningless = ['', 'n/a', 'na', 'none', 'null', 'self', 'employee', 'manager', 'missing']\\n",
    "        emp_title_clean = emp_title_clean.replace(meaningless, 'Unknown')\\n",
    "        self.top_emp_titles = emp_title_clean.value_counts().head(40).index.tolist()\\n",
    "        return self\\n",
    "    \\\\n",
    "    def transform(self, X):\\n",
    "        X = X.copy()\\n",
    "        # 1. FICO midpoint (industry standard) and risk categories\\n",
    "        X['fico_midpoint'] = (X['fico_range_low'] + X['fico_range_high']) / 2\\n",
    "        X['fico_category'] = pd.cut(X['fico_midpoint'], bins=[0, 580, 670, 740, 800, 850],\\n",
    "                                     labels=['Poor', 'Fair', 'Good', 'VeryGood', 'Exceptional']).astype(str)\\n",
    "        # 2. Credit utilization\\n",
    "        X['revol_util_ratio'] = X['revol_util'] / 100.0\\n",
    "        X['has_revol_bal'] = (X['revol_bal'] > 0).astype(int)\\n",
    "        # 3. Loan-to-income ratio (repayment capacity)\\n",
    "        X['loan_to_income'] = X['loan_amnt'] / (X['annual_inc'] + 1)\\n",
    "        # 4. Income features\\n",
    "        X['income_log'] = np.log1p(X['annual_inc'])\\n",
    "        X['income_category'] = pd.cut(X['annual_inc'], bins=[0, 40000, 70000, 100000, 150000, float('inf')],\\n",
    "                                       labels=['Low', 'Medium', 'High', 'VeryHigh', 'UltraHigh']).astype(str)\\n",
    "        # 5. Balance features\\n",
    "        X['total_bal_log'] = np.log1p(X['tot_cur_bal'].fillna(0))\\n",
    "        # 6. Mortgage indicator\\n",
    "        X['has_mortgage'] = (X['mort_acc'] > 0).astype(int)\\n",
    "        # 7. Inquiry intensity\\n",
    "        X['inq_total'] = X['inq_fi'] + X['inq_last_12m']\\n",
    "        X['high_inquiry'] = (X['inq_last_12m'] >= 4).astype(int)\\n",
    "        # 8. Delinquency and public record flags\\n",
    "        X['has_delinquency'] = (X['delinq_2yrs'] > 0).astype(int)\\n",
    "        X['has_public_record'] = (X['pub_rec'] > 0).astype(int)\\n",
    "        X['has_bankruptcy'] = (X['pub_rec_bankruptcies'] > 0).astype(int)\\n",
    "        X['has_collection'] = (X['collections_12_mths_ex_med'] > 0).astype(int)\\n",
    "        # 9. Handle missing 'mths_since' features (999 = never happened)\\n",
    "        for col in ['mths_since_last_record', 'mths_since_rcnt_il', \\\\n",
    "                     'mths_since_recent_bc', 'mths_since_recent_inq']:\\n",
    "            X[f'{col}_missing'] = X[col].isnull().astype(int)\\n",
    "            X[col] = X[col].fillna(999)\\n",
    "        X['mo_sin_old_il_acct'] = X['mo_sin_old_il_acct'].fillna(0)\\n",
    "        # 10. Credit depth and account ratios\\n",
    "        X['credit_depth'] = X['mo_sin_old_rev_tl_op'] + X['mo_sin_old_il_acct']\\n",
    "        X['open_to_total_ratio'] = X['open_acc'] / (X['total_acc'] + 1)\\n",
    "        # 11. Employment length (ordinal)\\n",
    "        emp_length_map = {'< 1 year': 0, '1 year': 1, '2 years': 2, '3 years': 3,\\n",
    "            '4 years': 4, '5 years': 5, '6 years': 6, '7 years': 7,\\n",
    "            '8 years': 8, '9 years': 9, '10+ years': 10}\\n",
    "        X['emp_length_years'] = X['emp_length'].map(emp_length_map).fillna(0)\\n",
    "        X['emp_length_missing'] = X['emp_length'].isnull().astype(int)\\n",
    "        # 12. Term numeric\\n",
    "        X['term_months'] = X['term'].map({' 36 months': 36, ' 60 months': 60}).fillna(36)\\n",
    "        # 13. Employment title grouping (reduce 35K+ unique values)\\n",
    "        emp_title_clean = X['emp_title'].fillna('Unknown').str.lower().str.strip()\\n",
    "        meaningless = ['', 'n/a', 'na', 'none', 'null', 'self', 'employee', 'manager', 'missing']\\n",
    "        emp_title_clean = emp_title_clean.replace(meaningless, 'Unknown')\\n",
    "        X['emp_title_grouped'] = emp_title_clean.apply(\\\\\\n",
    "            lambda x: x if x in self.top_emp_titles else 'Other')\\n",
    "        X['emp_title_missing'] = (emp_title_clean == 'Unknown').astype(int)\\n",
    "        # 14. ZIP code prefix (reduce cardinality)\\n",
    "        X['zip_prefix'] = X['zip_code'].str[:2]\\n",
    "        # Drop original columns that were engineered\\n",
    "        drop_cols = ['emp_title', 'emp_length', 'fico_range_low', 'fico_range_high', \\\\n",
    "                     'zip_code', 'term', 'revol_util']\\n",
    "        return X.drop(columns=[c for c in drop_cols if c in X.columns])\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Apply feature engineering\\n",
    "preprocessor_fe = LendingClubPreprocessor()\\n",
    "preprocessor_fe.fit(X_train)\\n",
    "X_train_fe = preprocessor_fe.transform(X_train)\\n",
    "X_val_fe = preprocessor_fe.transform(X_val)\\n",
    "X_test_fe = preprocessor_fe.transform(X_test)\\n",
    "test_fe = preprocessor_fe.transform(test_features)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(f\\"Features: {X_train.shape[1]} original -> {X_train_fe.shape[1]} after engineering\\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Preprocessing Pipeline\\n",
    "\\n",
    "All preprocessing is fit on training data ONLY to prevent leakage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "# SKLEARN PREPROCESSING PIPELINE (NO LEAKAGE)\\n",
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "def get_column_types(df):\\n",
    "    numeric = df.select_dtypes(include=[np.number]).columns.tolist()\\n",
    "    categorical = df.select_dtypes(include=['object', 'category']).columns.tolist()\\n",
    "    binary = [c for c in numeric if set(df[c].dropna().unique()).issubset({0, 1})]\\n",
    "    continuous = [c for c in numeric if c not in binary]\\n",
    "    return continuous, binary, categorical\\n",
    "\\n",
    "cont_cols, bin_cols, cat_cols = get_column_types(X_train_fe)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "preprocess_pipeline = ColumnTransformer(transformers=[\\n",
    "    ('num', Pipeline([('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='median')), \\\\n",
    "                      ('scaler', StandardScaler())]), cont_cols),\\n",
    "    ('bin', SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent'), bin_cols),\\n",
    "    ('cat', Pipeline([('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='constant', fill_value='Missing')),\\n",
    "                      ('onehot', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore', sparse_output=False, \\\\n",
    "                                               drop='first'))]), cat_cols)\\n",
    "], remainder='drop')\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# FIT ON TRAIN ONLY, then transform all sets\\n",
    "X_train_processed = preprocess_pipeline.fit_transform(X_train_fe)\\n",
    "X_val_processed = preprocess_pipeline.transform(X_val_fe)\\n",
    "X_test_processed = preprocess_pipeline.transform(X_test_fe)\\n",
    "test_processed = preprocess_pipeline.transform(test_fe)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(f\\"Processed shapes: Train={X_train_processed.shape} | Val={X_val_processed.shape} | Test={X_test_processed.shape}\\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Model 1-3: Gradient Boosting Models (XGBoost, LightGBM, CatBoost)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "We train three state-of-the-art gradient boosting models with optimized hyperparameters."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "# TRAIN 3 GRADIENT BOOSTING MODELS\\n",
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "def mape_score(y_true, y_pred):\\n",
    "    return np.mean(np.abs((y_true - y_pred) / y_true)) * 100\\n",
    "\\n",
    "def evaluate(model, X, y):\\n",
    "    preds = model.predict(X)\\n",
    "    return {\\n",
    "        'RMSE': np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y, preds)),\\n",
    "        'MAE': mean_absolute_error(y, preds),\\n",
    "        'MAPE': mape_score(y, preds),\\n",
    "        'R2': r2_score(y, preds)\\n",
    "    }\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# --- XGBoost ---\\n",
    "print(\\"Training XGBoost...\\")\\n",
    "model_xgb = xgb.XGBRegressor(\\n",
    "    n_estimators=1000, max_depth=6, learning_rate=0.05, subsample=0.8,\\n",
    "    colsample_bytree=0.8, reg_alpha=0.1, reg_lambda=1.0, min_child_weight=3,\\n",
    "    objective='reg:squarederror', random_state=42, n_jobs=-1, tree_method='hist')\\n",
    "model_xgb.fit(X_train_processed, y_train, eval_set=[(X_val_processed, y_val)], verbose=False)\\n",
    "results_xgb = evaluate(model_xgb, X_test_processed, y_test)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# --- LightGBM ---\\n",
    "print(\\"Training LightGBM...\\")\\n",
    "model_lgb = lgb.LGBMRegressor(\\n",
    "    n_estimators=1000, max_depth=8, learning_rate=0.05, num_leaves=64,\\n",
    "    subsample=0.8, colsample_bytree=0.8, reg_alpha=0.1, reg_lambda=1.0,\\n",
    "    min_child_samples=20, objective='regression', random_state=42, n_jobs=-1, verbose=-1)\\n",
    "model_lgb.fit(X_train_processed, y_train, eval_set=[(X_val_processed, y_val)])\\n",
    "results_lgb = evaluate(model_lgb, X_test_processed, y_test)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# --- CatBoost ---\\n",
    "print(\\"Training CatBoost...\\")\\n",
    "model_cb = cb.CatBoostRegressor(\\n",
    "    iterations=1000, depth=6, learning_rate=0.05, l2_leaf_reg=3.0,\\n",
    "    bagging_temperature=0.5, random_strength=1.0, border_count=128,\\n",
    "    loss_function='RMSE', random_seed=42, verbose=0, thread_count=-1)\\n",
    "model_cb.fit(X_train_processed, y_train, eval_set=(X_val_processed, y_val), verbose=0)\\n",
    "results_cb = evaluate(model_cb, X_test_processed, y_test)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Display results\\n",
    "comparison = pd.DataFrame({'XGBoost': results_xgb, 'LightGBM': results_lgb, 'CatBoost': results_cb}).round(4)\\n",
    "print(\\"\\\\nGradient Boosting Results on Temporal Test Set:\\")\\n",
    "print(comparison)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Model 4-5: Neural Network Models (FT-Transformer, Tab-MLP)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "We implement two neural network architectures to compare against gradient boosting:\\n",
    "- **FT-Transformer** (Gorishniy et al., 2021): Feature Tokenizer + Transformer Encoder\\n",
    "- **Tab-MLP**: Strong MLP baseline with layer normalization and residual-style connections"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "# NEURAL NETWORK MODELS\\n",
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "\\n",
    "NUM_FEATURES = X_train_processed.shape[1]\\n",
    "\\n",
    "class FTTransformer(nn.Module):\\n",
    "    \\\\n",
    "    Feature Tokenizer Transformer for Tabular Data (Gorishniy et al., 2021)\\n",
    "    Architecture: Feature Embedding -> CLS Token -> Transformer Encoder -> MLP Head\\n",
    "    \\\\n",
    "    def __init__(self, n_feat, d_token=16, n_blocks=2, n_heads=4, d_h=64, drop=0.1):\\n",
    "        super().__init__()\\n",
    "        self.num_embed = nn.Linear(n_feat, d_token)\\n",
    "        self.cls = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(1, 1, d_token))\\n",
    "        enc = nn.TransformerEncoderLayer(\\n",
    "            d_model=d_token, nhead=n_heads, dim_feedforward=d_h, dropout=drop,\\n",
    "            activation='gelu', batch_first=True, norm_first=True)\\n",
    "        self.transformer = nn.TransformerEncoder(enc, num_layers=n_blocks)\\n",
    "        self.head = nn.Sequential(\\n",
    "            nn.LayerNorm(d_token), nn.Linear(d_token, d_h), nn.GELU(),\\n",
    "            nn.Dropout(drop), nn.Linear(d_h, 1))\\n",
    "        for p in self.parameters():\\n",
    "            if p.dim() > 1: nn.init.xavier_uniform_(p)\\n",
    "    \\\\n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\\n",
    "        B = x.shape[0]\\n",
    "        tok = self.num_embed(x).unsqueeze(1)\\n",
    "        cls = self.cls.expand(B, -1, -1)\\n",
    "        out = self.transformer(torch.cat([cls, tok], dim=1))\\n",
    "        return self.head(out[:, 0, :]).squeeze(-1)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "class TabMLP(nn.Module):\\n",
    "    \\\\n",
    "    Strong MLP baseline with LayerNorm and GELU activations\\n",
    "    \\\\n",
    "    def __init__(self, inp, hid=[256, 128, 64], drop=0.2):\\n",
    "        super().__init__()\\n",
    "        layers = []\\n",
    "        prev = inp\\n",
    "        for h in hid:\\n",
    "            layers += [nn.Linear(prev, h), nn.LayerNorm(h), nn.GELU(), nn.Dropout(drop)]\\n",
    "            prev = h\\n",
    "        layers.append(nn.Linear(prev, 1))\\n",
    "        self.net = nn.Sequential(*layers)\\n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\\n",
    "        return self.net(x).squeeze(-1)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Prepare data loaders\\n",
    "Xt = torch.FloatTensor(np.array(X_train_processed, dtype=np.float32))\\n",
    "yt = torch.FloatTensor(np.array(y_train.values, dtype=np.float32)).unsqueeze(1)\\n",
    "Xv_t = torch.FloatTensor(np.array(X_val_processed, dtype=np.float32))\\n",
    "yv_t = torch.FloatTensor(np.array(y_val.values, dtype=np.float32)).unsqueeze(1)\\n",
    "Xte_t = torch.FloatTensor(np.array(X_test_processed, dtype=np.float32))\\n",
    "yte_t = torch.FloatTensor(np.array(y_test.values, dtype=np.float32)).unsqueeze(1)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "train_loader = DataLoader(TensorDataset(Xt, yt), batch_size=512, shuffle=True)\\n",
    "val_loader = DataLoader(TensorDataset(Xv_t, yv_t), batch_size=1024, shuffle=False)\\n",
    "test_loader = DataLoader(TensorDataset(Xte_t, yte_t), batch_size=1024, shuffle=False)\\n",
    "\\n",
    "print(f\\"Data loaders ready: {len(train_loader)} train batches\\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "# TRAIN NEURAL NETWORKS\\n",
    "# ============================================================\\n",
    "def train_nn(model, train_loader, val_loader, epochs=30, lr=1e-3, wd=1e-4, patience=8):\\n",
    "    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=lr, weight_decay=wd)\\n",
    "    scheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.ReduceLROnPlateau(optimizer, mode='min', factor=0.5, patience=4)\\n",
    "    criterion = nn.MSELoss()\\n",
    "    best_rmse, best_state, pc = float('inf'), None, 0\\n",
    "    for e in range(epochs):\\n",
    "        model.train()\\n",
    "        for xb, yb in train_loader:\\n",
    "            optimizer.zero_grad()\\n",
    "            loss = criterion(model(xb), yb.squeeze())\\n",
    "            loss.backward()\\n",
    "            torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), 1.0)\\n",
    "            optimizer.step()\\n",
    "        model.eval()\\n",
    "        vp, vt = [], []\\n",
    "        with torch.no_grad():\\n",
    "            for xb, yb in val_loader:\\n",
    "                vp.extend(model(xb).numpy())\\n",
    "                vt.extend(yb.squeeze().numpy())\\n",
    "        vrmse = np.sqrt(np.mean((np.array(vt)-np.array(vp))**2))\\n",
    "        scheduler.step(vrmse)\\n",
    "        if vrmse < best_rmse:\\n",
    "            best_rmse, best_state, pc = vrmse, {k:v.cpu().clone() for k,v in model.state_dict().items()}, 0\\n",
    "        else: pc += 1\\n",
    "        if (e+1) % 5 == 0:\\n",
    "            print(f\\"  Epoch {e+1}: val_rmse={vrmse:.4f}, best={best_rmse:.4f}\\")\\n",
    "        if pc >= patience:\\n",
    "            print(f\\"  Early stop at epoch {e+1}\\")\\n",
    "            break\\n",
    "    model.load_state_dict(best_state)\\n",
    "    return model\\n",
    "\\n",
    "def eval_nn(model, loader):\\n",
    "    model.eval()\\n",
    "    p, t = [], []\\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\\n",
    "        for xb, yb in loader:\\n",
    "            p.extend(model(xb).numpy())\\n",
    "            t.extend(yb.squeeze().numpy())\\n",
    "    p, t = np.array(p), np.array(t)\\n",
    "    return {\\n",
    "        'RMSE': np.sqrt(np.mean((t-p)**2)), 'MAE': np.mean(np.abs(t-p)),\\n",
    "        'MAPE': np.mean(np.abs((t-p)/t))*100,\\n",
    "        'R2': 1-np.sum((t-p)**2)/np.sum((t-t.mean())**2)}\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Train FT-Transformer\\n",
    "print(\\"Training FT-Transformer...\\")\\n",
    "ft_model = FTTransformer(NUM_FEATURES, d_token=16, n_blocks=2, n_heads=4, d_h=64, drop=0.1)\\n",
    "ft_model = train_nn(ft_model, train_loader, val_loader, epochs=30, lr=5e-3, wd=1e-4, patience=8)\\n",
    "ft_results = eval_nn(ft_model, test_loader)\\n",
    "print(f\\"FT-Transformer: RMSE={ft_results['RMSE']:.4f}, MAE={ft_results['MAE']:.4f}, MAPE={ft_results['MAPE']:.2f}%\\")\\n",
    "\\n",
    "# Train Tab-MLP\\n",
    "print(\\"\\\\nTraining Tab-MLP...\\")\\n",
    "mlp_model = TabMLP(NUM_FEATURES, hid=[256, 128, 64], drop=0.2)\\n",
    "mlp_model = train_nn(mlp_model, train_loader, val_loader, epochs=30, lr=1e-3, wd=1e-4, patience=8)\\n",
    "mlp_results = eval_nn(mlp_model, test_loader)\\n",
    "print(f\\"Tab-MLP: RMSE={mlp_results['RMSE']:.4f}, MAE={mlp_results['MAE']:.4f}, MAPE={mlp_results['MAPE']:.2f}%\\")"
   ]
